{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"BRAINSTORM PROVENANCE (2026-09-04, /rebar-brainstorm). Recorded via the local CLI because the configured MCP server timed out on every call this session (open bug 9ea3-7d07-ea55-4496).\n\nOperator decisions (in order): (1) all three seams MCP/CLI/library first-class; (2) notices are advisory + suppress only — no enforcement; scope = the notification system, mechanisms beyond notification are out (freeze, release/TTL, NOT-A-BUG registry → ideas burgundy-violet-narwhale, pure-dashing-sardine, aquarial-immoderate-schnauzer); (3) alerts file directly under the bug-creation contract, informed by this store's duplicate history — 24 canary-filed bugs, mostly serial duplicates from auto-close + re-fire (nine [binding-drift] in 14 days; two heartbeat bugs for a deliberately paused bridge) → eight anti-noise rules, recovery = comment never auto-close; (4) alert announcements go only to subscribed sessions, and runbook/guidance updates are in scope; (5) typed notice ticket type approved (schema impact enumerated on the notice child); design approved.\n\nResearch inputs (three reports + one critique, summarised in the child plans): server→client MCP push is dead on every target harness (Claude Code #7252/#36665/#45563 closed not-planned; Codex #15299/#17543/#18056 open; Cursor subscribe errors; OpenCode no resources) → boundary delivery (piggyback on tool results + hooks). Human trackers: auto-subscribe on assign + typed reason enum (GitHub Notifications API). Incident tools: curated-fingerprint dedup, firing→ack→resolved→regressed (Sentry), maintenance windows suppress notification not detection, 'the notice is the silence'. CI triage at scale (elastic-recheck, Treeherder, Sheriff-o-Matic): patchset-scoped vs trunk failures separated by where the job ran; poll-with-watermark is a legitimate topology; nobody auto-closes Actions-filed issues.\n\nCritique corrections adopted: MCP delivery is an appended text content block only (no outputSchema change; verified mcp 1.29.0 accepts a CallToolResult from a tool fn); session hint sub-partitions inside the authenticated principal, never across; transport Mcp-Session-Id never used as durable identity; stale claims flag-only; ingester batches writes; feed carries no comment prose (prompt-injection boundary).\n\nExecution order (depends_on recorded): diamond-miniscule-dassie → nephelite-sediment-apatosaur → {misleading-wizardly-yellowlegs, mysterious-zodiacal-fruitbat} → strained-lying-steed; aerobic-seraphic-blowfish after inbox + notice. Review in that order; the epic last."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788561808042070001,"uuid":"483d485b-151c-4dfd-8e79-4c8ab06499ee"}